From 190f6eb88335d8909b21f2e39a421f937523c0a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paperclip Agent <agent@togetherweown.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:56:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(meta): account-safe replay of Muse reasoning across
 tool turns

The Meta executor discarded Muse reasoning on every turn (GPT-only sanitizer), so the
model never saw its own earlier reasoning between tool calls. A naive pass-through works
for one account but fails in production: Claude Code resends the whole history, which mixes
envelopes from several pool accounts, and Meta rejects an envelope replayed through any
account but the one that issued it (400 'not issued to this caller').

When upstream.meta.reasoning-replay is enabled:
- responses (stream and non-stream, Anthropic thinking signature and Responses
  encrypted_content) carry meta#<account>#<envelope>;
- requests keep an envelope only when its tag names the credential selected for that
  request, with the tag stripped; every other or untagged envelope is dropped, which is the
  behavior without the feature;
- a request Meta still rejects as 'not issued to this caller' is retried once with every
  envelope removed (HTTP 4xx, and for non-streaming requests also an error event inside a 200
  body), so the rejection does not reach the client;
- each request that carried envelopes logs kept/dropped counts for measuring the hit rate.

Tests include a fake Meta upstream that enforces account binding behind a real Manager
that rotates accounts every turn, including 24-turn conversations across 2-4 accounts.
